The attached image, corresponding to Fig. 4 in the PDF, illustrates the enhanced uptake of antigen (OVA, green) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when adsorbed to Nano-11 (red) compared to soluble OVA alone. Confocal microscopy shows minimal OVA internalization when administered alone. However, with Nano-11-OVA complexes, both Nano-11 and OVA are efficiently phagocytized and colocalize within BMDCs, highlighting Nano-11's role in improving antigen delivery to these crucial antigen-presenting cells, a key mechanism for its adjuvant effect.